7. CONTRIBUTION-FORK EXCEPTION

If the Canonical Repository is hosted on a collaboration platform that uses
forks for pull requests, you may create and maintain a public platform fork
solely to propose contributions back to the Canonical Repository, provided:

(a) the fork retains this License and all legal notices;

(b) it is clearly identified as an unofficial contribution fork;

(c) it is used primarily for contribution branches and pull requests;

(d) no releases, installers, binaries, application packages, container images,
    package-registry publications, or other distributable artifacts are
    published from the fork;

(e) the fork is not marketed, operated, or maintained as an alternative
    LeoMiniGames distribution;

(f) no YoungLion trust mark or Official status is claimed; and

(g) contributions comply with the then-current CONTRIBUTOR_LICENSE_AGREEMENT.md
    when that document is required by the Canonical Repository.

This exception authorizes only the minimum public copying reasonably required
for contribution workflow. Platform terms that independently grant hosting
rights do not expand rights outside that platform.

8. PUBLISHER PACKAGE DEVELOPMENT PERMISSION

8.1 Independent Packages

The Licensor expressly permits creation and Distribution of a Publisher
Package under a license chosen by its Publisher, including a proprietary or
recognized open-source license, provided the Package:

(a) is independently developed;

(b) uses only Public Developer Interfaces and ordinary operating-system/runtime
    facilities;

(c) does not copy, embed, translate, adapt, or incorporate protected
    LeoMiniGames implementation except SDK/template material separately
    licensed to permit that use;

(d) does not require private/internal LeoMiniGames interfaces for essential
    operation; and

(e) does not misrepresent itself as part of the LeoMiniGames host.

A qualifying Publisher Package does not become covered by this License solely
because it interoperates with LeoMiniGames through a Public Developer Interface.

8.2 Publisher ownership

The Publisher retains ownership of rights it owns in its Publisher Package.
YoungLion does not acquire ownership merely because a Package is submitted,
reviewed, signed, hosted, cached, indexed, or distributed through the Platform.

8.3 Platform publication

Distribution through the YoungLion/LeoMiniGames Platform is additionally
governed by the current Developer / Publisher Distribution Terms and any
applicable Native/L3, commercial, privacy, security, or marketplace addendum.

8.4 No trust by license

A package license, manifest field, SDK header, local signature, or publication
request does not grant Trust Status. Platform trust is backend-authoritative.

